{"candidates":[{"content":"Replace the single-pass skeptical fixpoint with a two-phase 'commit-then-explain' semantics: after the least fixpoint stabilizes, run a polynomial-time traversal that requires every accepted node to have at least one minimal defeat tree whose leaves are committed roots, and every refuted node to have a defeat tree explaining the defeat. Nodes failing the explanation check are demoted to suspended. This preserves determinism and polynomial cost because the traversal is on the already-computed labels, and it makes reinstatement a constructive by-product rather than an implicit label.","typicality":0.35,"neighbours":["SRC_003","SRC_004"]},{"content":"Introduce a horizon parameter k on attack edges: an edge is active only if its warrant chain has length at most k. Compute the grounded extension for each k and define the eventual skeptical status as the stable value for all sufficiently large k. This yields a graded notion of groundedness that can be decided in polynomial time by iterating k up to the node count, preserves determinism, and makes reinstatement a property of eventual stabilization; it can be criticized for changing the fixed point on cycles and for possibly requiring large k.","typicality":0.15,"neighbours":["SRC_002","SRC_005"]},{"content":"Make the grounded extension context-sensitive by partitioning attack edges into warrant contexts and computing the skeptical fixpoint as the meet over all contexts, using a shared label vector to keep cost polynomial. Acceptance must survive every context, which strengthens the skeptical commitment and preserves determinism, but it is conservative and may be criticized for discarding context-specific evidence that should be admissible.","typicality":0.25,"neighbours":["SRC_001","SRC_002"]},{"content":"Reformulate the skeptical semantics as a finite two-player dialectical game: a conjecture is accepted iff the proponent has a winning strategy in a DAG game where opponent attacks are answered by defeat trees rooted at committed roots; solve by backward induction in polynomial time. This preserves determinism and polynomial cost, makes reinstatement a natural game-theoretic consequence, and enforces committed-root validity by construction, but it may be criticized for being a notational variant of the fixpoint rather than an expansion.","typicality":0.4,"neighbours":["SRC_003","SRC_004"]},{"content":"Add a second-order consistency layer: after the skeptical fixpoint, encode the admissible extensions consistent with the labels as a polynomial-size propositional formula, and require that the least model of that formula under a fixed variable order matches the fixpoint. This gives a logical characterization that exposes hidden dependencies and preserves determinism and polynomial cost, but it adds no new inferential power and may be criticized as an expensive verification step with limited strengthening.","typicality":0.2,"neighbours":["SRC_006","SRC_008"]}]}